cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BioBridge, please also cite SpliceAI (Jaganathan et al., Cell 2019,
  doi:10.1016/j.cell.2018.12.015), and give the BioBridge source revision recorded
  in your results CSV (column biobridge_commit).
title: BioBridge
abstract: >-
  A macOS application that runs the unmodified SpliceAI model locally on small sets
  of GRCh38 variants through a browser interface, with masked and raw scores,
  deterministic explanations and provenance-complete CSV export. Experimental
  research software; not a diagnostic.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - alias: rinatrizvanov
keywords:
  - SpliceAI
  - splicing
  - variant effect prediction
  - bioinformatics
  - macOS
